{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "טעמו", :translit "ta'amo", :gloss "its taste"} {:he "והיה טעמו כטעם לשד השמן", :translit "vehaya ta'amo k'ta'am lashad hashamen", :gloss "and its taste was like the taste of rich cream"} {:he "שאנן מואב מנעוריו ושקט הוא על שמריו על כן עמד טעמו בו", :translit "shanah moav mine'urav v'shaket hu al shmarav al ken amad ta'amo bo", :gloss "Moab has been at ease from his youth and settled on his lees therefore its taste stood in it"} {:he "וישנו את טעמו", :translit "v'yashnu et ta'amo", :gloss "and its taste changed"} {:he "בשנותו את טעמו גבי דוד", :translit "b'shanoto et ta'amo gabei david", :gloss "when its taste changed regarding David"} {:he "מואב שהיה שקט עמד טעמו", :translit "moav shehayah shaket amad ta'amo", :gloss "Moab who was settled its taste stood"} {:he "אבל דוד שגלה ממקום למקום בשנותו את טעמו", :translit "aval david shegalah mim'kom l'makom b'shanoto et ta'amo", :gloss "but David who went into exile from place to place changed its taste"} {:he "ודור המדבר אף ע\"פ שגלו ממקום למקום לא שינו את טעמן בשביל המן", :translit "v'dor hamidbar af al pi shegalu mim'kom l'makom lo shinu et ta'aman bishvil haman", :gloss "and the wilderness generation even though they went from place to place did not change their taste on account of the manna"} {:he "וטעמו", :translit "u'ta'amo", :gloss "and its taste"} {:he "שלא נתנה תורה אלא לאוכלי המן", :translit "shelo nitnah torah ella l'ochlei haman", :gloss "for the Torah was given only to the eaters of the manna"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Gezerah shavah linking טעמו in Numbers 11:8 to טעמו in Jeremiah 48:11 via shared lemma"} {:kind :gematria, :a "טעמו", :b "ד'"}], :frame {:text "Jeremiah 48:11 describes Moab as שאנן מנעוריו ושקט הוא על שמריו, at ease from youth and settled on its lees, a prophecy of Moab's complacency. The midrash reads the word טעמו in Numbers 11:8 about the manna as linking to עמד טעמו בו in Jeremiah 48:11: wine left undisturbed on its dregs retains its flavor, while wine moved from place to place loses taste. The wilderness generation, though constantly journeying, did not lose the consistent taste of the manna. A tradition states that Torah was given only to eaters of the manna (Mekhilta de-Rabbi Yishmael, Beshallah, Vayehi section 1; Yoma 75b).", :sources ["Jeremiah 48:11" "Numbers 11:8" "Yoma 75b" "Mekhilta de-Rabbi Yishmael Beshallah 1"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Gezerah shavah linking טעמו in Numbers 11:8 to טעמו in Jeremiah 48:11 via shared lemma", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :gematria, :a "טעמו", :a-value 125, :b "ד'", :b-value 4, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? false}], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:28:22.234375231Z", :model "glm-5.2"}